    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202-a1">

                <pb facs="0301" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg227"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p>We have to inform you that the form of passport to be issued to any Japanese,
                    without distinction of class, either official or merchant, who may wish to
                    travel abroad for purposes of study or trade, has been determined upon, and
                    herewith send you a specimen copy of the same, which we request you to
                    communicate to your government. We have further to say that such passports, when
                    issued at Kanagawa, Nagasaki, or Hakodate, shall be partly stamped with a seal
                    of the local governments, the counterpart of the seal to remain on record at the
                    port of issue.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Stated with respect and esteem, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-06">the 29th day of the ninth month
                            of the second year of Ke W., (November 6, 1866</date>.)</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>INOWEYE KAWATSI NO KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MATSU DAIRA SUWO NO KAMI.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>MATSU DAIRA NIU NO KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency R. B. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Valkenburgh,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States of
                            America.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
